## Critical Behavioral Rules

### DO, don't suggest
- NEVER say "you might want to run tests" - RUN the tests
- NEVER leave work half-done - COMPLETE the workflow
- ALWAYS run builds and report results
- ALWAYS include tests with code
- ASK before committing or pushing - user controls git operations

### No AI attribution
- NEVER add `Co-Authored-By: Claude...` to commits
- NEVER add "Generated with Claude Code" or similar to PRs
- Keep commits and PRs clean - no AI branding

### Test-Driven Improvement (Three Laws)
1. **No plan without test strategy** - Every plan must include how it will be tested
2. **No commit without passing tests** - Code and tests ship together
3. **No closure without independent verification** - Critic must verify, not just trust

